@startuml
' M2 - Use case diagram (section 3.1.1)
' Actors match section 3.1.2.
' UC02, UC03, UC04 are the payment choice inside UC01 (one is chosen at step 3).
' UC05 (Print Ticket) is always included in UC01.
' UC06 (Cancel / Refund) extends UC01 only when a failure or cancel happens.
title Ticket Vendor Machine (TVM) - Use Case Diagram

left to right direction

actor "Passenger" as P
actor "Maintenance Staff" as MS
actor "Operator" as OP
actor "Payment Gateway" as PG
actor "Bank" as BK
actor "Momo" as MO
actor "VNPay" as VN
actor "ZaloPay" as ZP

rectangle "Ticket Vendor Machine (TVM)" {
  usecase "UC01\nBuy a Ticket" as UC01
  usecase "UC02\nPay by Credit Card" as UC02
  usecase "UC03\nPay by QR Code" as UC03
  usecase "UC04\nPay by Digital Wallet" as UC04
  usecase "UC05\nPrint Ticket" as UC05
  usecase "UC06\nCancel Purchase / Refund" as UC06
  usecase "UC07\nRefill Paper & Maintain TVM" as UC07
  usecase "UC08\nMonitor Machine Status" as UC08
}

' Primary actors
P -- UC01
P -- UC02
P -- UC03
P -- UC04
P -- UC06
MS -- UC07
OP -- UC08

' Secondary actors
PG -- UC02
PG -- UC03
PG -- UC04
PG -- UC06

' Payment providers are specialisations of the Payment Gateway actor
PG <|-- BK
PG <|-- MO
PG <|-- VN
PG <|-- ZP

' Relationships
UC01 ..> UC05 : <<include>>
UC06 ..> UC01 : <<extend>>\n(failure or cancel)

note right of UC01
  Step 3: passenger chooses one of
  UC02, UC03 or UC04.
end note

@enduml
